To be pendatic, that's not particularly accurate. You may know the distinction,
but it may mislead a newbie.

Monsters will never walk on Elbereth that has either you STANDING on it
or AT LEAST one object on it. Thus, if you engrave Elbereth on open space,
monsters will walk right across it. Either you have to be standing on Elbereth
or there at least has to be 1 object on the Elbereth'ed square for Elbereth
to work.

Also note:
1. Humans and quasi-humans and blinded (not blind) monsters don't respect
Elbereth.
2. Peacefuls and pets don't respect Elbereth.

Complete stash security! (Not recommended for general use):

Pickaxe a hole. Put chest in. Seal the hole. Fire-engrave Elbereth. Put
another boulder over Elbereth.

